# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deny-all allowlist (DIL house style).
#
# Everything is ignored by default; a short allowlist adds back the few file
# types that belong in version control; a block of hard denials then outranks
# the allowlist. Last matching pattern wins, so ORDER IN THIS FILE MATTERS --
# add new allowances to the allowlist section, never below the denials.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. When in doubt, leave it ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Deny everything ...
*

# 2. ... but descend into directories, so the allowlist below can reach files.
!*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Allowlist: the only file types this repo tracks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!*.py
!*.md
!.gitignore
!.gitkeep
!.env.example
# Anchored to the repo root: an unanchored !requirements.txt would also
# un-ignore a stray 2-code/requirements.txt at any depth.
!/requirements.txt
!/LICENSE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Hard denials. These sit below the allowlist on purpose, so they win.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- TWO DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS FROM THE DIL REFERENCE .gitignore -----------
#
# (a) *.html is denied GLOBALLY, including under 3-output/.
#     The pipeline's report.html is not a rendered summary: it embeds the
#     ENTIRE dataset as inline JSON -- real village names, operator usernames,
#     free-text grievances. It is a data file that happens to have a viewer
#     attached, so it is treated as data, not as an output artifact.
#
# (b) *.csv is denied GLOBALLY. The reference allows CSV under 3-output/**,
#     but every CSV this pipeline writes is record-level data, and
#     data_dictionary.csv is not an exception: its `example` column is
#     populated from live rows.
#
# Neither of these is an oversight. Do not "fix" them. See AGENTS.md
# > Deliberate deviations from the DIL convention.
*.html
*.csv

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- OS / editor / tooling cruft -------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. 1-data/ mirrors Box. NOTHING under it is ever committed except the
#    directory structure, the sidecar .md documentation and .gitkeep markers.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
1-data/**
!1-data/**/
!1-data/**/*.md
!1-data/**/.gitkeep
